  Quote(id: 374, text: "We are what we repeatedly do. Excellence, then, is not an act but a habit.", author: "Will Durant", category: "Work"),
  Quote(id: 375, text: "Far and away the best prize that life offers is the chance to work hard at work worth doing.", author: "Theodore Roosevelt", category: "Work"),
  Quote(id: 376, text: "Great things in business are never done by one person. They're done by a team of people.", author: "Steve Jobs", category: "Work"),
  Quote(id: 377, text: "The master has failed more times than the beginner has even tried.", author: "Stephen McCranie", category: "Work"),
  Quote(id: 378, text: "Worry is a misuse of the imagination.", author: "Dan Zadra", category: "Fear"),
  Quote(id: 379, text: "The mind that is anxious about future events is miserable.", author: "Seneca", category: "Fear"),
  Quote(id: 380, text: "Every noble work is at first impossible.", author: "Thomas Carlyle", category: "Work"),
  Quote(id: 381, text: "But ye, brethren, be not weary in well doing.", author: "2 Thessalonians 3:13", category: "Bible"),
  Quote(id: 382, text: "Our greatest danger in life is in permitting the urgent things to crowd out the important.", author: "Charles E. Hummel", category: "Work"),
  Quote(id: 383, text: "He who has begun is half done. Dare to be wise; begin!", author: "Horace", category: "Action"),
  Quote(id: 384, text: "Security is mostly a superstition. Avoiding danger is no safer in the long run than outright exposure.", author: "Helen Keller", category: "Courage"),
  Quote(id: 385, text: "Talent hits a target no one else can hit; genius hits a target no one else can see.", author: "Arthur Schopenhauer", category: "Success"),
  Quote(id: 386, text: "The greatest mistake you can make in life is to be continually fearing you will make one.", author: "Elbert Hubbard", category: "Courage"),
  Quote(id: 387, text: "The difference between the impossible and the possible lies in a man's determination.", author: "Tommy Lasorda", category: "Goals"),
  Quote(id: 388, text: "The secret of success is constancy to purpose.", author: "Benjamin Disraeli", category: "Goals"),
  Quote(id: 389, text: "Even the darkest night will end and the sun will rise.", author: "Victor Hugo", category: "Motivation"),
  Quote(id: 390, text: "No medicine cures what happiness cannot.", author: "Gabriel Garcia Marquez", category: "Happiness"),
  Quote(id: 391, text: "Adversity has the effect of eliciting talents, which in prosperous circumstances would have lain dormant.", author: "Horace", category: "Perseverance"),
