  Quote(id: 554, text: "Rejoice evermore. Pray without ceasing. In every thing give thanks: for this is the will of God in Christ Jesus concerning you.", author: "1 Thessalonians 5:16-18", category: "Bible"),
  Quote(id: 555, text: "I want to put a ding in the universe.", author: "Steve Jobs", category: "Goals"),
  Quote(id: 556, text: "Make no little plans; they have no magic to stir men's blood.", author: "Daniel Burnham", category: "Goals"),
  Quote(id: 557, text: "No one is useless in this world who lightens the burdens of another.", author: "Charles Dickens", category: "Wisdom"),
  Quote(id: 558, text: "Jump, and you will find out how to unfold your wings as you fall.", author: "Ray Bradbury", category: "Courage"),
  Quote(id: 559, text: "The man who has no imagination has no wings.", author: "Muhammad Ali", category: "Dreams"),
  Quote(id: 560, text: "Plans are only good intentions unless they immediately degenerate into hard work.", author: "Peter Drucker", category: "Action"),
  Quote(id: 561, text: "When we are no longer able to change a situation, we are challenged to change ourselves.", author: "Viktor Frankl", category: "Wisdom"),
  Quote(id: 562, text: "Courage is grace under pressure.", author: "Ernest Hemingway", category: "Fear"),
  Quote(id: 563, text: "Be less curious about people and more curious about ideas.", author: "Marie Curie", category: "Wisdom"),
  Quote(id: 564, text: "Enjoy the little things, for one day you may look back and realize they were the big things.", author: "Robert Brault", category: "Happiness"),
  Quote(id: 565, text: "Commit thy way unto the LORD; trust also in him; and he shall bring it to pass.", author: "Psalms 37:5", category: "Bible"),
  Quote(id: 566, text: "The roots of education are bitter, but the fruit is sweet.", author: "Aristotle", category: "Wisdom"),
  Quote(id: 567, text: "If you want to make an easy job seem mighty hard, just keep putting off doing it.", author: "Olin Miller", category: "Action"),
  Quote(id: 568, text: "Keep your fears to yourself, but share your courage with others.", author: "Robert Louis Stevenson", category: "Courage"),
  Quote(id: 569, text: "Cheerfulness is the best promoter of health and is as friendly to the mind as to the body.", author: "Joseph Addison", category: "Happiness"),
  Quote(id: 570, text: "We do not remember days, we remember moments.", author: "Cesare Pavese", category: "Life"),
  Quote(id: 571, text: "You must expect great things of yourself before you can do them.", author: "Michael Jordan", category: "Success"),
  Quote(id: 572, text: "Hide not your talents. They for use were made. What's a sundial in the shade?", author: "Benjamin Franklin", category: "Work"),
  Quote(id: 573, text: "Don't be afraid your life will end; be afraid that it will never begin.", author: "Grace Hansen", category: "Fear"),
  Quote(id: 574, text: "In the long run, men hit only what they aim at. Therefore, they had better aim at something high.", author: "Henry David Thoreau", category: "Goals"),
  Quote(id: 575, text: "Joy is the simplest form of gratitude.", author: "Karl Barth", category: "Happiness"),
  Quote(id: 576, text: "Nothing is impossible. The word itself says 'I'm possible'!", author: "Audrey Hepburn", category: "Motivation"),
  Quote(id: 577, text: "Gratitude is not only the greatest of virtues, but the parent of all others.", author: "Cicero", category: "Happiness"),
  Quote(id: 578, text: "Gold medals aren't really made of gold. They're made of sweat, determination, and a hard-to-find alloy called guts.", author: "Dan Gable", category: "Success"),
  Quote(id: 579, text: "Perseverance is more prevailing than violence; and many things which cannot be overcome when they are together, yield themselves up when taken little by little.", author: "Plutarch", category: "Perseverance"),
  Quote(id: 580, text: "The good life is a process, not a state of being.", author: "Carl Rogers", category: "Life"),
  Quote(id: 581, text: "Action may not always bring happiness; but there is no happiness without action.", author: "Benjamin Disraeli", category: "Action"),
  Quote(id: 582, text: "Every adversity, every failure, every heartache carries with it the seed of an equal or greater benefit.", author: "Napoleon Hill", category: "Perseverance"),
