  Quote(id: 851, text: "Striving for excellence motivates you; striving for perfection is demoralizing.", author: "Harriet Braiker", category: "Work"),
  Quote(id: 852, text: "Loss is nothing else but change, and change is Nature's delight.", author: "Marcus Aurelius", category: "Life"),
  Quote(id: 853, text: "Our truest life is when we are in dreams awake.", author: "Henry David Thoreau", category: "Dreams"),
  Quote(id: 854, text: "Two are better than one; because they have a good reward for their labour.", author: "Ecclesiastes 4:9", category: "Bible"),
  Quote(id: 855, text: "Dreams, if they're any good, are always a little bit crazy.", author: "Ray Charles", category: "Dreams"),
  Quote(id: 856, text: "Whether you think you can, or you think you can't, you're right.", author: "Henry Ford", category: "Success"),
  Quote(id: 857, text: "The greatest use of a life is to spend it on something that will outlast it.", author: "William James", category: "Life"),
  Quote(id: 858, text: "Life is like a landscape. You live in the midst of it but can describe it only from the vantage point of distance.", author: "Charles Lindbergh", category: "Life"),
  Quote(id: 859, text: "I don't dream at night, I dream all day; I dream for a living.", author: "Steven Spielberg", category: "Dreams"),
  Quote(id: 860, text: "Dreams are illustrations from the book your soul is writing about you.", author: "Marsha Norman", category: "Dreams"),
  Quote(id: 861, text: "Be careful for nothing; but in every thing by prayer and supplication with thanksgiving let your requests be made known unto God.", author: "Philippians 4:6", category: "Bible"),
  Quote(id: 862, text: "If you don't like something, change it. If you can't change it, change your attitude.", author: "Maya Angelou", category: "Wisdom"),
  Quote(id: 863, text: "Heaven never helps the man who will not act.", author: "Sophocles", category: "Action"),
  Quote(id: 864, text: "When you have to make a choice and don't make it, that is in itself a choice.", author: "William James", category: "Action"),
  Quote(id: 865, text: "Aim for the moon. If you miss, you may hit a star.", author: "W. Clement Stone", category: "Goals"),
  Quote(id: 866, text: "We suffer more often in imagination than in reality.", author: "Seneca", category: "Fear"),
  Quote(id: 867, text: "Do the hard jobs first. The easy jobs will take care of themselves.", author: "Dale Carnegie", category: "Work"),
  Quote(id: 868, text: "No man ever steps in the same river twice, for it's not the same river and he's not the same man.", author: "Heraclitus", category: "Wisdom"),
  Quote(id: 869, text: "The pessimist complains about the wind; the optimist expects it to change; the realist adjusts the sails.", author: "William Arthur Ward", category: "Wisdom"),
  Quote(id: 870, text: "Arriving at one goal is the starting point to another.", author: "John Dewey", category: "Goals"),
  Quote(id: 871, text: "Failure is an option here. If things are not failing, you are not innovating enough.", author: "Elon Musk", category: "Fear"),
  Quote(id: 872, text: "In the beginner's mind there are many possibilities, but in the expert's there are few.", author: "Shunryu Suzuki", category: "Wisdom"),
  Quote(id: 873, text: "Never let the future disturb you. You will meet it, if you have to, with the same weapons of reason which today arm you against the present.", author: "Marcus Aurelius", category: "Fear"),
  Quote(id: 874, text: "Dreams are extremely important. You can't do it unless you can imagine it.", author: "George Lucas", category: "Dreams"),
