  Quote(id: 878, text: "The world needs dreamers and the world needs doers. But above all, the world needs dreamers who do.", author: "Sarah Ban Breathnach", category: "Dreams"),
  Quote(id: 879, text: "The future is not something we enter. The future is something we create.", author: "Leonard I. Sweet", category: "Dreams"),
  Quote(id: 880, text: "I am not afraid of tomorrow, for I have seen yesterday and I love today.", author: "William Allen White", category: "Courage"),
  Quote(id: 881, text: "Formal education will make you a living; self-education will make you a fortune.", author: "Jim Rohn", category: "Work"),
  Quote(id: 882, text: "Life loves to be taken by the lapel and told: 'I'm with you kid. Let's go.'", author: "Maya Angelou", category: "Life"),
  Quote(id: 883, text: "Don't let what you cannot do interfere with what you can do.", author: "John Wooden", category: "Action"),
  Quote(id: 884, text: "Age is no barrier. It's a limitation you put on your mind.", author: "Jackie Joyner-Kersee", category: "Motivation"),
  Quote(id: 885, text: "Procrastination is the thief of time.", author: "Edward Young", category: "Action"),
  Quote(id: 886, text: "The world is round and the place which may seem like the end may also be only the beginning.", author: "Ivy Baker Priest", category: "Life"),
  Quote(id: 887, text: "Without labor nothing prospers.", author: "Sophocles", category: "Work"),
  Quote(id: 888, text: "Success is a state of mind. If you want success, start thinking of yourself as a success.", author: "Joyce Brothers", category: "Success"),
  Quote(id: 889, text: "The critical ingredient is getting off your butt and doing something.", author: "Nolan Bushnell", category: "Action"),
  Quote(id: 890, text: "I am not afraid of storms, for I am learning how to sail my ship.", author: "Louisa May Alcott", category: "Fear"),
  Quote(id: 891, text: "For which cause we faint not; but though our outward man perish, yet the inward man is renewed day by day.", author: "2 Corinthians 4:16", category: "Bible"),
  Quote(id: 892, text: "Those who bring sunshine into the lives of others cannot keep it from themselves.", author: "J.M. Barrie", category: "Happiness"),
  Quote(id: 893, text: "Life is a festival only to the wise.", author: "Ralph Waldo Emerson", category: "Life"),
  Quote(id: 894, text: "Out of difficulties grow miracles.", author: "Jean de La Bruyère", category: "Motivation"),
  Quote(id: 895, text: "Dreams are today's answers to tomorrow's questions.", author: "Edgar Cayce", category: "Dreams"),
  Quote(id: 896, text: "I'd rather regret the things I've done than regret the things I haven't done.", author: "Lucille Ball", category: "Fear"),
  Quote(id: 897, text: "First say to yourself what you would be; and then do what you have to do.", author: "Epictetus", category: "Action"),
  Quote(id: 898, text: "Happiness is a how; not a what. A talent, not an object.", author: "Hermann Hesse", category: "Happiness"),
  Quote(id: 899, text: "It's kind of fun to do the impossible.", author: "Walt Disney", category: "Dreams"),
  Quote(id: 900, text: "He who is contented is rich.", author: "Lao Tzu", category: "Happiness"),
  Quote(id: 901, text: "Ability may get you to the top, but it takes character to keep you there.", author: "John Wooden", category: "Success"),
  Quote(id: 902, text: "A man is not old until regrets take the place of dreams.", author: "John Barrymore", category: "Dreams"),
  Quote(id: 903, text: "Before anything else, preparation is the key to success.", author: "Alexander Graham Bell", category: "Success"),
  Quote(id: 904, text: "I am the master of my fate, I am the captain of my soul.", author: "William Ernest Henley", category: "Motivation"),
  Quote(id: 905, text: "The human spirit is stronger than anything that can happen to it.", author: "C.C. Scott", category: "Motivation"),
  Quote(id: 906, text: "Let your light so shine before men, that they may see your good works, and glorify your Father which is in heaven.", author: "Matthew 5:16", category: "Bible"),
  Quote(id: 907, text: "Remember that failure is an event, not a person.", author: "Zig Ziglar", category: "Fear"),
  Quote(id: 908, text: "Do the thing you fear, and the death of fear is certain.", author: "Ralph Waldo Emerson", category: "Fear"),
  Quote(id: 909, text: "Charity suffereth long, and is kind; charity envieth not; charity vaunteth not itself, is not puffed up,", author: "1 Corinthians 13:4", category: "Bible"),
  Quote(id: 910, text: "There is only one success: to be able to spend your life in your own way.", author: "Christopher Morley", category: "Success"),
  Quote(id: 911, text: "In three words I can sum up everything I've learned about life: it goes on.", author: "Robert Frost", category: "Perseverance"),
  Quote(id: 912, text: "Life is a long lesson in humility.", author: "J.M. Barrie", category: "Life"),
  Quote(id: 913, text: "Do not fear mistakes. There are none.", author: "Miles Davis", category: "Fear"),
  Quote(id: 914, text: "This above all: to thine own self be true.", author: "William Shakespeare", category: "Wisdom"),
  Quote(id: 915, text: "Ambition is the path to success. Persistence is the vehicle you arrive in.", author: "Bill Bradley", category: "Goals"),
  Quote(id: 916, text: "Cause me to hear thy lovingkindness in the morning; for in thee do I trust: cause me to know the way wherein I should walk; for I lift up my soul unto thee.", author: "Psalms 143:8", category: "Bible"),
  Quote(id: 917, text: "It is the chiefest point of happiness that a man is willing to be what he is.", author: "Erasmus", category: "Happiness"),
  Quote(id: 918, text: "You can't build a reputation on what you are going to do.", author: "Henry Ford", category: "Action"),
  Quote(id: 919, text: "The cave you fear to enter holds the treasure you seek.", author: "Joseph Campbell", category: "Fear"),
  Quote(id: 920, text: "Empty your mind, be formless, shapeless, like water.", author: "Bruce Lee", category: "Motivation"),
  Quote(id: 921, text: "Luck is what happens when preparation meets opportunity.", author: "Seneca", category: "Success"),
  Quote(id: 922, text: "Wherefore comfort yourselves together, and edify one another, even as also ye do.", author: "1 Thessalonians 5:11", category: "Bible"),
  Quote(id: 923, text: "Content makes poor men rich; discontent makes rich men poor.", author: "Benjamin Franklin", category: "Happiness"),
  Quote(id: 924, text: "Begin with the end in mind.", author: "Stephen R. Covey", category: "Goals"),
  Quote(id: 925, text: "Nothing great was ever achieved without enthusiasm.", author: "Ralph Waldo Emerson", category: "Motivation"),
  Quote(id: 926, text: "Take chances, make mistakes. That's how you grow. Pain nourishes your courage. You have to fail in order to practice being brave.", author: "Mary Tyler Moore", category: "Fear"),
  Quote(id: 927, text: "A man of genius makes no mistakes. His errors are volitional and are the portals of discovery.", author: "James Joyce", category: "Fear"),
  Quote(id: 928, text: "Happy he who learns to bear what he cannot change.", author: "Friedrich Schiller", category: "Happiness"),
  Quote(id: 929, text: "Do the best you can until you know better. Then when you know better, do better.", author: "Maya Angelou", category: "Wisdom"),
  Quote(id: 930, text: "The butterfly counts not months but moments, and has time enough.", author: "Rabindranath Tagore", category: "Life"),
  Quote(id: 931, text: "If you aim at nothing, you will hit it every time.", author: "Zig Ziglar", category: "Goals"),
  Quote(id: 932, text: "Education is the most powerful weapon which you can use to change the world.", author: "Nelson Mandela", category: "Wisdom"),
  Quote(id: 933, text: "Contentment is natural wealth, luxury is artificial poverty.", author: "Socrates", category: "Happiness"),
  Quote(id: 934, text: "The art of life is to know how to enjoy a little and to endure much.", author: "William Hazlitt", category: "Life"),
  Quote(id: 935, text: "Pleasure in the job puts perfection in the work.", author: "Aristotle", category: "Success"),
  Quote(id: 936, text: "Always do your best. What you plant now, you will harvest later.", author: "Og Mandino", category: "Work"),
  Quote(id: 937, text: "Champions aren't made in gyms. Champions are made from something they have deep inside them: a desire, a dream, a vision.", author: "Muhammad Ali", category: "Success"),
  Quote(id: 938, text: "Our greatest weakness lies in giving up. The most certain way to succeed is always to try just one more time.", author: "Thomas Edison", category: "Perseverance"),
  Quote(id: 939, text: "Life is available only in the present moment.", author: "Thich Nhat Hanh", category: "Life"),
  Quote(id: 940, text: "God is our refuge and strength, a very present help in trouble.", author: "Psalms 46:1", category: "Bible"),
  Quote(id: 941, text: "Champions keep playing until they get it right.", author: "Billie Jean King", category: "Motivation"),
  Quote(id: 942, text: "He who fears he will suffer, already suffers because he fears.", author: "Michel de Montaigne", category: "Fear"),
  Quote(id: 943, text: "Know what you want to do, hold the thought firmly, and do every day what should be done, and every sunset will see you that much nearer to your goal.", author: "Elbert Hubbard", category: "Goals"),
  Quote(id: 944, text: "Talent wins games, but teamwork and intelligence win championships.", author: "Michael Jordan", category: "Work"),
  Quote(id: 945, text: "Trust in the LORD with all thine heart; and lean not unto thine own understanding. In all thy ways acknowledge him, and he shall direct thy paths.", author: "Proverbs 3:5-6", category: "Bible"),
  Quote(id: 946, text: "A good goal is like a strenuous exercise; it makes you stretch.", author: "Mary Kay Ash", category: "Goals"),
  Quote(id: 947, text: "The soul becomes dyed with the color of its thoughts.", author: "Marcus Aurelius", category: "Wisdom"),
  Quote(id: 948, text: "Courage starts with showing up and letting ourselves be seen.", author: "Brene Brown", category: "Courage"),
  Quote(id: 949, text: "I like the dreams of the future better than the history of the past.", author: "Thomas Jefferson", category: "Dreams"),
  Quote(id: 950, text: "Don't watch the clock; do what it does. Keep going.", author: "Sam Levenson", category: "Motivation"),
  Quote(id: 951, text: "Call unto me, and I will answer thee, and shew thee great and mighty things, which thou knowest not.", author: "Jeremiah 33:3", category: "Bible"),
  Quote(id: 952, text: "The successful man will profit from his mistakes and try again in a different way.", author: "Dale Carnegie", category: "Success"),
  Quote(id: 953, text: "Ask yourself whether you are happy, and you cease to be so.", author: "John Stuart Mill", category: "Happiness"),
